  "_evidence": "Mapping for the AsiaBeautyBrief legacy import (abb-launch W5). No site id, no image host: those live in the owner-held overlay ~/abb-private/overlay.json. From the owner's read-only discovery 22-10-26 (415 rows: 322 published, 75 archived, 18 draft, 0 rejected; legacy site slug asiabeautybrief; 398 featured images all on mbolvnwkmkeroqmvbvmt.supabase.co; media_assets 0 rows) and owner defaults D7. FINAL: (1) categories: the old sections equal the new pillars except supply-side -> supply; every old sub-section slug exists unchanged in the new taxonomy (market-moves 238, deals-money 35, ingredients-actives 26, medical-aesthetics 24, people 22, policy-regulation 14, beauty-culture 12, packaging 8, beauty-tech 6, trend-radar 6, korea 6, sustainability 5, new-noteworthy 5, china 4, global-lens 1, india-south-asia 1), so they pass through; briefing with no sub-section (2) goes to the pillar only. No Press Room rows today; press-room/* is mapped to the single-home pressroom pillar (no sub-section) only in case a catch-up run meets one. (2) authors: spread over the 5 staff names by a stable slug hash (mode slugHash); the legacy byline (ABB Newsroom) is never kept. (3) tags: only the 57 approved tags of scripts/lib/abb-taxonomy.ts, matched by slugified legacy tag; the rest dropped. (4) SEO dropped (the importer never writes legacy seo; the column is read only to count it in the report). (5) featured image -> tenant media on R2, credit from featured_image_credit. (6) draft -> draft, published -> published. (7) old article URL is /article/{slug} on the apex host, same as the new site. PROVISIONAL (owner decision pending): status.map archived (D7 default: import as published; alternatives draft or SKIP like AER), media.bodyImages (drop until 01-discover-abb.sql reports the body image count).",
